  "summary": "Proposed v0.1.2-proposed.1 corrective pass preserves the existing architecture/source layout. Reproduced all six supplied correctness findings, then fixed per-path impact, typed task-input closure, immutable revision-bound receipt history/current applicability, schema-driven u64 checks, running-response identity and explicit CLI prompts. Added regression-tested command metadata, terminal/shell/output contracts, DE-W019 and scoped protocol/acquisition/writer gates. The icon report is attributed source material; no unavailable asset or permission is adopted. Actual final suite: 144 tests ran, 142 passed, two symlink tests skipped. Structural checks: 840; 71 concepts, 144 requirements, 36 work units, 27 schemas. All 36 planned AIDE exports pass passive pinned-schema validation. Current and inherited results are retained separately. This handoff was captured before the authorized commit/push and does not claim publication, owner acceptance or native implementation.",
